WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.420 --> 00:00:05.760
Libertarians just want to take care of themselves
and not take care of other people.

00:00:05.760 --> 00:00:08.200
You must hate the poor you must love the rich.

00:00:08.200 --> 00:00:09.760
You must be a pacifist.

00:00:09.760 --> 00:00:12.220
They're different from what you are.

00:00:12.220 --> 00:00:16.200
I want everybody to die from tainted liquor
or from food poisoning.

00:00:18.780 --> 00:00:22.840
For Reason I'm Justin Monticello, I'm here
in New Hampshire for PorcFest

00:00:22.840 --> 00:00:26.660
or the Porcupine Freedom Festival put on by
the free state project.

00:00:26.660 --> 00:00:31.600
It's an annual week long gathering of liberty
minded individuals from anarchists to libertarians.

00:00:31.600 --> 00:00:34.060
I'm here to ask people what's one thing you're
tired of hearing

00:00:34.060 --> 00:00:36.360
when you tell other people your political
beliefs?

00:00:36.360 --> 00:00:39.640
Sometimes people say things like 'oh anarchists
are all violent.

00:00:39.640 --> 00:00:41.940
Without government warlords would take over
society.

00:00:41.940 --> 00:00:46.740
It bothers me because with government warlords
have already taken over society.

00:00:46.740 --> 00:00:48.680
My mom she pretty much just asks

00:00:48.680 --> 00:00:51.340
'why are you a libertarian? we're supposed
to be Democrats.'

00:00:51.340 --> 00:00:54.500
They're like 'normally black people aren't
libertarians.'

00:00:54.500 --> 00:00:59.580
But I'm like 'nah some people are just way
different than others.

00:00:59.580 --> 00:01:01.880
Being a Democrat it's kind of a trap you know?

00:01:01.880 --> 00:01:03.740
They tell you one thing and then do something
else.

00:01:03.740 --> 00:01:08.760
I really dislike when people say 'well Venezuela
didn't fall because it wasn't real socialism.'

00:01:08.760 --> 00:01:10.140
You know, marijuana's evil.

00:01:10.140 --> 00:01:12.320
How will people build public roads without
government.

00:01:12.320 --> 00:01:18.260
The taxes that you pay as a business are the
price that you pay to be a part of a civilized society.

00:01:18.260 --> 00:01:21.400
I grew up in the north of Mexico, my parents
are cattle ranchers

00:01:21.400 --> 00:01:23.620
and no one maintained the road, no government
did.

00:01:23.620 --> 00:01:28.300
The local ranchers got together, decided to
pool their funds to hire a tractor to go pave the road.

00:01:28.300 --> 00:01:29.620
So who will build the roads?

00:01:29.620 --> 00:01:31.940
Well I've already answered that question in
my own lifetime.

00:01:34.800 --> 00:01:38.219
Definitely I'm transitioning into a crypto
based company.

00:01:38.220 --> 00:01:41.460
I'm really tired of hearing all of people's
fear excuses.

00:01:50.520 --> 00:01:55.220
People that say that the bailouts that we
did, you know, that these banks were too big to fail.

00:01:55.220 --> 00:01:58.160
The rich don't pay for this stuff, you know,
it's regular people.

00:01:58.160 --> 00:02:00.720
You know the people that can basically least
afford it.

00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:06.460
I shouldn't object to paying 26 thousand dollars
a year in taxes to run a small restaurant

00:02:06.460 --> 00:02:09.620
so that I can have employees that can barely
read.

00:02:13.700 --> 00:02:19.140
What I'm most tired of hearing is that I don't
care about the environment, charity

00:02:19.160 --> 00:02:22.660
just because I don't want government doing
anything about it.

00:02:22.660 --> 00:02:28.080
Small changes in the amount of decentralization
or centralization changes how happy our society is,

00:02:28.080 --> 00:02:30.480
how healthy our children are, how long you'll
live, that sort of thing.

00:02:30.480 --> 00:02:34.200
I actually care more than the person who's
not willing to question

00:02:34.200 --> 00:02:36.780
how they go about accomplishing those goals.

00:02:36.780 --> 00:02:39.520
I'd say I'm tired of maybe a lack of openness?

00:02:39.520 --> 00:02:42.200
You know, what are your philosophies rather
than your labels.

00:02:42.200 --> 00:02:46.600
I know the only thing that the universe really
cares about is how we treat each other.

00:02:46.600 --> 00:02:49.540
Using coercive government, just, it's time
to move beyond that.

00:02:49.540 --> 00:02:52.840
There's much less harmful, much more efficient
ways of doing that.

00:02:52.840 --> 00:02:54.440
I mean I like being free.

